Package: OccurrenceCleaner
Title: Fast Quality Checks for Species Occurrence Records
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", , "gilles.colling051@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066"))
Description: An extension of 'CoordinateCleaner' (Zizka et al. 2019
    <doi:10.1111/2041-210X.13152>) tailored to large-scale species occurrence
    data. Flags common problems in occurrence records, such as coordinates at
    country centroids, capitals or biodiversity institutions, zero or equal
    coordinates, records at sea, in the wrong country or outside the species
    range, duplicates, outliers within a species, and datasets with converted
    or gridded coordinates, with the test definitions and default buffers
    of 'CoordinateCleaner' apart from documented differences. It also reads
    the quality warnings GBIF attaches to each record, the basis of record and
    the establishment means, and checks records at sea or on land against the
    habitat of their genus from the Interim Register of Marine and Nonmarine
    Genera. Records are flagged and kept, and users choose
    afterwards which flags to filter on. Data frames of a few million records
    are flagged in seconds, and GBIF snapshots of billions of records are
    processed by reading Parquet files in chunks.
